# Nested repositories. Git does not nest: adding one of these would record a
# bare pointer to a commit with none of its content, which looks tracked and is
# not. Each has its own history and its own GitHub remote, so they stay
# independent and this repo covers only what nothing else does.
/temple-product-generator/
/temple-ref-finder/
/humanizer-stack/
# Leading slashes are load-bearing: unanchored, these patterns match at every
# level and would also swallow .claude/skills/temple-product-generator/ and
# .claude/skills/temple-ref-finder/, which are exactly the skills CLAUDE.md
# points at. They went missing from the first staging attempt that way.

# Audit screenshots. The REPORT.md and manifest.json are the thinking and are
# tracked; the shots are 29MB of evidence that re-running the audit reproduces.
audits/*/shots/

# Claude Code scratch: worktrees are checkouts of the sub-repos above, and
# settings.local.json is per-machine.
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/settings.local.json

.DS_Store
.env
.venv*/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
